&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;#LI-Hybrid&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;AXS Japan GK, of AXS Group, LLC is a subsidiary of AEG and millions of tickets every year for 500+ partners across North America, Europe, and Asia, from venues like the O2 in London and the Red Rocks Amphitheatre in Denver to the teams like the Los Angeles Kings, Vegas Golden Knights, and Houston Rockets. Headquartered in Downtown Los Angeles, California, AXS employs more than 500 professionals in multiple locations worldwide, including US offices in Charlotte, Cleveland, Dallas, Denver, Tempe and Las Vegas and international offices in London, Melbourne, Stockholm, Berlin, Paris, and Tokyo. At each location you’ll find a team of dedicated, diverse employees (we’ve dubbed ourselves “Fanatix”) who create groundbreaking products and services in a fun, fast-paced environment. Since our founding in 2011 and as part of Anschutz Entertainment Group (AEG Worldwide), we’ve consistently pushed the industry forward and improved experiences for fans, making it easier than ever to discover events, find the perfect seats, and enjoy unforgettable live entertainment, and we continue to lead the evolution of our industry today.&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;AXS is thrilled to be expanding its operations in our Tokyo office. This move comes as our company continues to grow its global footprint. In Japan, AXS Tickets functions as the operating company, while AXS Japan focuses on development and corporate functions.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;The Finance Director will lead and develop a small team based in Tokyo and will take ownership of the day-to-day running of the core finance function. Responsible for all accounting processes and systems ranging from technical accounting, cash flow management, client settlements, financial reporting, payroll, and budgets. You will assume responsibility for AXS Japan finance and work closely with the Managing Director advising on strategy and expansion. You will have a unique blend of capabilities. You will be as comfortable leading and developing a growing team who can power and support our expanding business as you are managing the core, day-to-day finance function and advising on strategy. You will love working at pace and will quickly get to the heart of an issue, propose and deliver an appropriate solution. You will know the importance of meeting deadlines, have a meticulous eye for detail and recognize when to jump in and get your hands dirty. You will be a credible business partner and a great communicator - supporting and challenging the business simultaneously. You will thrive working as part of a passionate, busy team who love what they do.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Accountabilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Overall control and responsibility for all financial aspects of the business and provide insight into Company strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create AXS Japan budget and forecasting as required by Managing Director&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Promote the business interests of AXS offices, whilst keeping within local and regional guidelines and legislation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for consolidation and audits, including working closely with internal and external advisors to ensure full compliance and timely tax and statutory filings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for ensuring alignment with the Global Finance teams. Working closely with the VP Finance - APAC and ensuring best global financial practice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate corporate finance and manage Company policies including overall responsibility for treasury management, particularly robust control over our client related cashflows and settlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Activities and Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and coordinate the annual budget and monthly re-forecasts process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with other departments to help plan and manage budgets throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce timely, accurate monthly management accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve systems and processes within the team and the Company to ensure strong and appropriate levels of financial control and risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all accounts payable, receivable, expenses, fraud and payroll systems are operating effectively and in line with Company requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the Company’s treasury function, assessing implications of business transactionsand manage banking relationships with our advisors and partners as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor cashflow, always ensuring there are enough funds for anticipated payments, including client settlements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with all relevant external reporting requirements and timetables including Corporation Tax, Consumption Tax, and statutory accounting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute fully to the development of the Company strategy across all areas of the business, challenging assumptions, and decision-making as appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the monthly payroll process to ensure that everyone is paid accurately and on time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel as may be required by the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills and Experience we’re seeking&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;CPA(Japan), CPA(US), ACA or CIMA preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;SME desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent strategic and analytical thinking&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of leading and managing a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evidence of operating at both strategic and operational levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced skills in Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to form close working relationships with senior management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Self-motivated and ability to handle high levels of pressure and critical decision-making&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work with multiple currencies and cultures across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience within fast paced growing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with JD Edwards desirable&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Languages: Native Japanese level speaker along with conversational English ability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Note: This job description is not intended to be all-inclusive. The Finance Director may be required to perform other related duties as assigned.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s in it for You?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The opportunity to play an integral role in expanding our global footprint&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extraordinary People – we’re not kidding!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meaningful Mission - Helping revolutionize an industry and deliver better experiences for fans and clients around the world.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunities for learning and leveling up through training and education reimbursement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location: &lt;/strong&gt;SOA TOWER, Shibuya A 10-minute walk from Shibuya Station or a 5-minute walk from Omotesando Station&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Established: &lt;/strong&gt;AXS Japan GK in 2020, AXS Group LLC established in 2011, AEG established in 1999&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Number of Employees:&lt;/strong&gt; AXS Japan GK = 8, AXS Tickets = 11 AXS Group, LLC globally = 1000&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AXS connects fans with the artists and teams they love. Each year we sell millions of tickets to thousands of incredible events – from concerts and festivals to sports and theater – at some of the most iconic venues in the world. Since our founding in 2011, we’ve consistently pushed the industry forward and improved experiences for fans, making it easier than ever to discover events, find the perfect seats, and enjoy unforgettable live entertainment, and we continue to lead the evolution of our industry today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re passionate about improving the fan experience and providing game-changing solutions for our clients, and we’re always looking for smart, motivated people to help make it happen. Bring your enthusiasm, your big ideas, and your desire to team up with some of the best and brightest in technology and entertainment. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Financial Settlement Specialist will play a role in the financial operations, ensuring accurate and timely settlement of events through the AXS ticketing platform. The role involves collaborating with internal teams, reconciling financial data, and providing exceptional support to both clients and venue partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run weekly reports from our AXS ticketing system to track revenues and liabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with reconciliation and financial analysis projects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our clients’ finance teams to ensure the timely and accurate financial settlement of events using the AXS ticketing platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calculate settlement amounts and fees for events sold in the AXS system to support payments to clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide reporting to our clients to support settlement payments and invoices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist our venue partners with reporting and financial issues related to AXS ticketing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to client inquiries about settlement and finance issues with prompt and clear communication.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Accurately audit our fee structures based on client contracts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with our accounting team to produce journal entries that provide general ledger support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications (ALL)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AA/AS Degree (2-year) (BA/BS Degree Preferred) Finance, Accounting, or relevant field of study&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years years of experience in Accounting or Finance OR Live Event or Ticketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient knowledge of MS Excel required, including pivot tables and some macros.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Creative problem solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage projects and deadlines simultaneously.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective customer service and communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of financial reconciliation processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with auditing procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
