&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE COMPANY&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AXS is a global ticketing provider for venues, sports clubs, and live events, delivering innovative ticketing, data, and marketing solutions. In Germany, AXS plays a central role in the live entertainment ecosystem through its close connection with Anschutz Entertainment Group, Inc. (AEG), the independent, globally operating entertainment group behind many of the country’s most prominent venues. These include Berlin’s Uber Arena and Uber Eats Music Hall, as well as Hamburg’s Barclays Arena.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AXS is responsible for ticketing for AEG Presents, one of the world’s leading organizers of tours, festivals, and concerts. Fans of internationally renowned artists such as Taylor Swift, Ed Sheeran, Kylie Minogue, Katy Perry, and BLACKPINK rely on AXS to access unforgettable live events, including globally celebrated festivals such as Coachella and major concert series across Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of AXS Europe, we are a preferred ticketing partner for some of the largest venues and festivals across the continent. Using the latest technology, we seamlessly guide fans through every stage of the event life cycle - from ticket discovery and purchase to venue access and beyond. Our revolutionary digital platforms are designed to deliver an intuitive, high-quality user experience that makes live entertainment more accessible and enjoyable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Founded in 2011, AXS has consistently driven innovation within the ticketing industry, improving how fans discover events, find the perfect seats, and connect with live experiences. From our European headquarters in London and across our teams throughout Germany, wider Europe, and the US, we continue to evolve the industry with dedicated, diverse teams working in a dynamic, fast‑paced environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are passionate about enhancing the fan experience and providing game‑changing solutions for our partners and clients in Germany and beyond. With a strong culture, exciting benefits, and a shared love for live entertainment, we’re always looking for motivated people ready to bring new ideas and help keep the world cheering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As People &amp;amp; Culture Business Partner for Germany, you will play a key role in supporting local leaders and teams while partnering closely with European and Global People &amp;amp; Culture leadership to implement and uphold AXS’s people strategy. You will act as a trusted advisor to the German business, balancing local market needs, German labour law requirements, and cultural nuances with European and global initiatives.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role has a strong focus on culture building, organisational development, integration, and harmonisation, supporting AXS as it continues to evolve and grow across Germany and Europe.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are a trusted People &amp;amp; Culture professional with strong expertise across the employee lifecycle and a solid understanding of German labour law within a European and global context. You are comfortable navigating complex people topics - such as organisational change, integration, and harmonisation - and partnering closely with leaders, works councils, and People &amp;amp; Culture colleagues across regions and time zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are highly organised, proactive, and confident engaging with diverse stakeholder groups, from frontline managers to senior executives. You excel at translating People &amp;amp; Culture strategies, policies, and data into clear, practical guidance that enables leaders to make informed, people‑centric decisions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You care deeply about building inclusive, high‑performing cultures, supporting employee engagement and development, and embedding AXS values into everyday behaviours and ways of working. Above all, you are motivated by the opportunity to contribute to a growing, international People &amp;amp; Culture function - helping shape an evolving organisation while balancing local needs with European and global priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic HR &amp;amp; Business Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with German leaders and stakeholders to translate global and European People &amp;amp; Culture strategies into impactful local initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support executives and senior leaders on people, culture, and organisational topics aligned with AXS’s business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary People &amp;amp; Culture interface for AXS Germany, reporting directly to the VP, People &amp;amp; Culture, Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with European and Global People &amp;amp; Culture leadership to ensure alignment, consistency, and best‑practice sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture, Integration &amp;amp; Harmonisation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively shape and strengthen AXS culture in Germany in line with global values, behaviours, and engagement ambitions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and support integration and harmonisation initiatives across Germany, ensuring consistency in people processes, policies, and ways of working while respecting local requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and deliver culture, engagement, and employee experience initiatives, including follow‑up actions from annual engagement surveys.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support change and transformation initiatives, acting as a coach and sounding board for leaders and teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Lifecycle &amp;amp; Organisational Development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and support the full employee lifecycle in Germany - from workforce planning, recruitment, onboarding, and development through to offboarding.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Further develop learning, talent, and development initiatives, including performance management, feedback processes, compensation, and bonus cycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support succession planning and talent reviews in partnership with European People &amp;amp; Culture colleagues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Employer Branding&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and support recruitment activities in Germany to enable sustainable growth and attract top talent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with hiring managers on recruitment strategy, selection, and decision‑making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to and implement local employer branding initiatives that strengthen AXS’s reputation as an employer of choice in Germany.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;HR Operations, Reporting &amp;amp; Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Finance to support payroll and benefits administration, including data validation, monthly payroll inputs, benefits enrolment and lifecycle management (joiners, changes, leavers), reporting, and ensuring accuracy, compliance, and a positive employee experience across all related processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global People &amp;amp; Culture and local teams on HR reporting, including headcount, personnel metrics, and cost reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise managers on German labour law, employee relations, and works council matters where applicable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with local labour laws and internal policies while supporting the harmonisation of HR practices across Europe.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;KEY SKILLS &amp;amp; EXPERIENCE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Several years of experience as an HR Business Partner, HR Generalist, or in a comparable role within a dynamic, fast‑paced environment, with strong expertise across the full employee lifecycle including recruitment and talent management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience supporting organisational change, transformation, and organisational development initiatives, with the ability to identify practical, business‑aligned solutions to emerging challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship‑building skills with a demonstrated ability to establish trust and credibility with leaders, managers, and employees at all levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident communicator with excellent verbal and written skills, able to influence stakeholders positively, navigate complexity, and collaborate effectively across teams and functions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organised with a structured, detail‑oriented approach; able to manage multiple priorities, handle high volumes of work, and maintain accuracy under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Team‑oriented mindset with a track record of contributing to shared goals, fostering collaboration, and building strong professional relationships across departments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong affinity for HR systems, data, and tools, with the ability to leverage insights to support decision‑making and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional German and English language skills, with experience working in international environments (ideally with US‑based teams), combined with a flexible, positive attitude and a genuine passion for the live entertainment industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DESIRABLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;A degree in Human Resources, Business Administration, Labour Law, or a related field, or a recognised HR qualification.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;AXS connects fans with the artists and teams they love. Each year we sell millions of tickets to thousands of incredible events – from concerts and festivals to sports and theater – at some of the most iconic venues in the world. Since our founding in 2011, we’ve consistently pushed the industry forward and improved experiences for fans, making it easier than ever to discover events, find the perfect seats, and enjoy unforgettable live entertainment, and we continue to lead the evolution of our industry today.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re passionate about improving the fan experience and providing game-changing solutions for our clients, and we’re always looking for smart, motivated people to help make it happen. Bring your enthusiasm, your big ideas, and your desire to team up with some of the best and brightest in technology and entertainment. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AXS is seeking a Lead Software Engineer – Full Stack to lead the design and development of our core ticketing platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will lead full-stack work across user interfaces, back-end services, APIs, and integrations. The role combines hands-on development with technical leadership, architecture, and team guidance in a complex enterprise environment. You’ll own initiatives end-to-end on front-end and back-end, drive technical direction, and partner with Product, Design, and engineering to ship secure, scalable software for high-demand, global use cases.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You’ll Be Doing&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain front-end and back-end features for web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead full-stack architecture and design reviews; author or review technical design as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set standards for code quality, security, performance, accessibility, and scalability on UI and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build APIs, business logic, and integrations that support strong user experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support agile delivery: planning, estimation, backlog breakdown, risk and blocker management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion testing, CI/CD, observability, and operational practices for apps and services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers, lead code reviews, and improve documentation and knowledge sharing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What to Bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Required&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of professional software development experience, including technical leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong front-end experience: HTML, CSS, JavaScript, TypeScript; frameworks such as React or Next.js; modern UI architecture, accessibility, and responsive design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong back-end experience: C# and .NET Core; building APIs, services, and business logic that power web applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to own work across front-end and back-end, not only one layer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of API design, integrations, and modern application architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience optimizing UI performance and service performance/reliability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead engineers, set engineering standards, and drive work from concept through production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent verbal and written communication; strong analytical and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AWS; Terraform, Docker, Kubernetes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;PostgreSQL, Redis, or similar data stores; Node.js.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design systems, CI/CD, distributed or event-driven patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;At AXS, we are dedicated to building a diverse,&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;inclusive&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;and authentic workplace, so if&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;you’re&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;excited about this role but&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;can&#39;t&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&quot;check every box&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;&quot;&amp;nbsp;in&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;the job description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be the right candidate for this or other roles.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;EOP SCXW129143701 BCX0&quot; data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:false,&amp;quot;201341983&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559738&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:200,&amp;quot;335559740&amp;quot;:276}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
